---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CaratIcon from '../assets/carat.svg';
---

<Layout pageTitle="Directory of Spooky & Horror-themed Businesses & Locations">
	<section id="about" class="site-padding">
		<h1>About</h1>
		<p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur, adipisicing elit. Ratione deserunt quis, animi inventore nemo autem eos eius ea! Voluptate deserunt distinctio pariatur dignissimos veritatis aliquid tempore sed. Officiis, asperiores debitis?</p>
	</section>

  <section id="faq" class="faq-section site-padding">
    <h2 class="type-step-3 font-display distortion-filter">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <ul class="faq-list" role="list">
      <li>
        <details>
          <summary>
            <div class="summary-text">
              Why "Spoooky" with three "O"s?
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="tag tag--square summary-icon">
                <CaratIcon />
              </div>
            </div>
          </summary>
          <div>
            <p>Because spooky.biz was super expensive, and three "O"s is fun! But if you wanna buy it and donate it to us, <a href="mailto:hellospoookybiz@gmail.com" target="_blank">let us know</a>!</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </li>
      <li>
        <details>
          <summary>
            <div class="summary-text">
              Why only businesses, and not haunted places, etc?
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="tag tag--square summary-icon">
                <CaratIcon />
              </div>
            </div>
          </summary>
          <div>
            <p>There are already plenty of directories for haunted places (like, reportedtly haunted buildings, etc), as well as for haunted attractions. If that's what you're looking for, check out the following:</p>
            <ul class="bullet-list">
              <li><a href="https://www.thescarefactor.com/" target="_blank">The Scare Factor</a></li>
              <li><a href="https://www.haunts.com/haunted-places/" target="_blank">Haunts.com</a></li>
              <li><a href="https://hauntedus.com/" target="_blank">HauntedUS.com</a></li>
              <li><a href="https://www.hauntworld.com/" target="_blank">HauntedWorld.com</a></li>
              <li><a href="https://frightmaps.com/" target="_blank">Frightmaps</a></li>
              <li><a href="https://dotsonmaps.com/dots/eerie/paranormal" target="_blank">Haunted Places Around the World: Dots on Maps</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>
      </li>
      <li>
        <details>
          <summary>
            <div class="summary-text">
              Was this thing built with AI?
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="tag tag--square summary-icon">
                <CaratIcon />
              </div>
            </div>
          </summary>
          <div>
            <p>No. I'm a professional web developer, and while there are some AI coding tools built into the code editor I use (namely, autocomplete suggestions), I built the site myself (with <a href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank">Astro</a> and Google Sheets, if you're curious), and at the launch of the site in August 2026, I personally looked up and hand-entered all of the data for every single business in the directory.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </li>
      <li>
        <details>
          <summary>
            <div class="summary-text">
              What qualifies as "spooky"?
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="tag tag--square summary-icon">
                <CaratIcon />
              </div>
            </div>
          </summary>
          <div>
            <p>Yeah, sometimes it's not obvious. I just try to make a judgement on whether a significant portion of the business is themed or selling things that are clearly in the realm of spooky. So maybe it's a collectibles shop that doesn't exclusively sell horror collectibles, but it's still got enough to make a horror fan want to check out—I'll count that, for example.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </li>
      <li>
        <details>
          <summary>
            <div class="summary-text">
              Why isn't my business, or business I'm a fan of listed?
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="tag tag--square summary-icon">
                <CaratIcon />
              </div>
            </div>
          </summary>
          <div>
            <p>We may just not know about it yet—please go fill out <a href="https://forms.gle/ddq9AjSiJLYuQQ4B8" target="_blank">the submission form</a>, and if it's a good fit, we'll add it!</p>
            <p>If you've done that and it's still not listed, here's a few reasons it may not have been included:</p>
            <ul class="bullet-list">
              <li>It didn't meet the criteria outlined in the submission form</li>
              <li>It just didn't feel quite spooky enough</li>
              <li>It didn't meet our ethical standards. The niche of 'oddities' definitely has some overlap with what we list, but if the business showcases items that we consider to be exploitative, or in bad taste, we're not gonna list it. (example: real human remains, etc)</li>
              <li>The business owner is known to be a bigot, fascist, or some other kind of shitty person.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>If you think we've made a mistake, please <a href="mailto:hellospoookybiz@gmail.com" target="_blank">let us know</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </li>
      <li>
        <details>
          <summary>
            <div class="summary-text">
              Can I pay to have my business listed first?
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="tag tag--square summary-icon">
                <CaratIcon />
              </div>
            </div>
          </summary>
          <div>
            <p>Nah. At least not at this moment. Part of the reason I started this project was because some alternatives were inundated with ads and paid listings. I'm not saying I'll never do it, but I'd need to find a way to do it that doesn't feel annoying. <a href="mailto:hellospoookybiz@gmail.com" target="_blank">Let me know</a> if you have any ideas!</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </li>
      <li>
        <details>
          <summary>
            <div class="summary-text">
              Who's behind this?
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="tag tag--square summary-icon">
                <CaratIcon />
              </div>
            </div>
          </summary>
          <div>
            <p>Me—Hi! I'm <a href="https://www.mattsoria.com/" target="_blank">Matt Soria</a>. I'm a photographer and web developer, but I'm also a huge fan of all things Horror, Halloween, and spoooky! I built this site because every time I travel, I'm always looking for new, spoooky spots to check out, and I felt like existing directories were, no offense, a bit lacking. So I built my own!</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.faq-section {
		max-width: 60ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
		margin-block-start: var(--space-3xl);
	}

	.faq-list {
		margin-block-start: var(--space-l);

		> li {
			border-block-start: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-fg-primary) 50%, transparent);

			&:last-child {
					border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-fg-primary) 50%, transparent);
			}

			details {
				&[open] {
					.summary-icon svg {
						transform: rotate(180deg);
					}
				}
			}
		}

		summary {
			display: flex;
			cursor: pointer;
			align-items: start;
			gap: var(--space-2xs);
			justify-content: space-between;
			padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-3xs);

			.summary-text {
				text-wrap: pretty;
				font-size: var(--step-1);
			}

			&:hover,
			&:focus-visible {
				background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-fg-primary) 10%, transparent);
			}

			+ div {
				padding-block: var(--space-xs) var(--space-l);
			}
		}
	}
</style>